# =============================================================================
# DeepSeek-V4-Flash -- antirez IQ2XXS (~81 GiB) + MTP speculative decoding
# =============================================================================
# The fastest coherent DeepSeek-V4 setup measured on this box (docs/RESULTS.md
# section 7). Two ideas stacked:
#
#   1. FIT-IN-VRAM.  This antirez quant is ~81 GiB, so the *whole* model lives in
#      the 96 GiB of VRAM -- no expert spill to DDR5. That alone is ~3.4x the
#      MXFP4 quant (which spills 145 GiB and is pinned to ~20 tok/s by DDR5
#      bandwidth). Coherence was checked: 17x23=391 with working, correct
#      Rayleigh-scattering answer, valid Fibonacci code. Good for a 2-bit quant.
#
#   2. MTP (Multi-Token Prediction).  A separate 5.5 GiB predictor companion
#      (philpax/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-MTP-bf16.gguf) drafts tokens the target then
#      verifies in one pass. MEASURED +25% here (75 -> 94 tok/s at 32k;
#      87 tok/s at the 65536 default below).
#
#   MEASURED:  65536 ctx, f16 KV -> 92.8 GiB VRAM used, ~87 tok/s, drafts
#   accepted. For comparison, 2x DGX Spark on this model is 37-40 tok/s.
#
#   ./serve.sh deepseek-v4-flash-mtp
#   ./serve-deepseek-v4-flash-antirez-IQ2XXS-gpu-mtp-65k.sh   (same, convenience wrapper)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The fit-in-VRAM antirez quant (single-file GGUF, not a split).
: "${IK_MODEL_GLOB:=/home/matt/.lmstudio/models/antirez/deepseek-v4-gguf/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-IQ2XXS-w2Q2K-AProjQ8-SExpQ8-OutQ8-chat-v2-imatrix.gguf}"

: "${IK_ALIAS:=deepseek-v4-flash-mtp}"

# --- context ----------------------------------------------------------------
# 65536 is the sweet spot for THIS setup. The math: the 81 GiB target + its KV
# fills VRAM to ~87 GiB, and the 5.5 GiB MTP draft needs the rest. At 131072 the
# target+KV grows past ~90 GiB and the draft no longer fits -> CUDA OOM (VERIFIED
# to abort). So with MTP on, 65536 is the practical ceiling here.
#
# Need the full 131072? Drop MTP and use the plain `deepseek-v4-flash` profile
# with this same antirez model -- it fits at 128k (~90 GiB) and does ~69 tok/s.
# The trade is real: 65k @ 87 tok/s (MTP) vs 128k @ 69 tok/s (no MTP).
: "${IK_CTX:=65536}"

# --- placement: MANUAL, no --fit -------------------------------------------
# CRITICAL: --fit cannot co-account for the draft model. With the target filling
# VRAM, the draft's own auto-fit fails with "Unable to auto-fit model" no matter
# how big --fit-margin is. So we place the target manually: IK_FIT=0 with no
# -ncmoe/-ot means serve.sh passes a bare `-ngl 99` -- all layers on the GPU,
# which is exactly right because this quant already fits. The draft then takes
# the remaining VRAM (see -md/-ngld below).
: "${IK_FIT:=0}"

# --- KV cache: f16 (MLA) ----------------------------------------------------
# The MLA cache is an already-compressed latent -- keep it f16, do not quantize.
: "${IK_CTK:=f16}"
: "${IK_CTV:=f16}"

# Smaller micro-batch trims the CUDA compute buffer; helps the tight VRAM budget
# (92.8 GiB used at 65536 leaves only ~4 GiB free).
: "${IK_UBATCH:=512}"

# --- MTP draft + DeepSeek specifics -----------------------------------------
# -md   the predictor-only companion (5.5 GiB). MTP is NOT baked into any quant;
#       every DeepSeek-V4 GGUF strips the predictor tail, so it must be supplied
#       separately. Download: philpax/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-MTP-Only-GGUF.
# -ngld 99   keep the whole tiny draft on the GPU.
# -cd 8192   cap the draft's own KV so it doesn't inherit the full target ctx.
# --spec-type mtp:n_max=1,p_min=0.0   one MTP head, accept greedily.
# Plus the usual DeepSeek-V4 flags (MLA mode 3, fused DSA indexer, reasoning).
: "${IK_MTP_DRAFT:=/home/matt/.lmstudio/models/philpax/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-MTP-Only-GGUF/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-MTP-bf16.gguf}"
: "${IK_EXTRA_ARGS:=-mla 3 -fidx --reasoning-format deepseek -md ${IK_MTP_DRAFT} -ngld 99 -cd 8192 --spec-type mtp:n_max=1,p_min=0.0}"
